message: "If you use this research, please cite this archived version."
title: "The smallest graph with a nonunimodal independence polynomial"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "The minimum order of a finite simple graph with a nonunimodal independence polynomial is 15, even for connected graphs. An explicit witness attains 15. The lower bound combines colored clique-vector inequalities with a finite integer certificate, without enumerating graphs."
